#!/usr/local/bin/dyalogscript
⍝ Phase 6 (ADR D14): exercises examples/toy-jsonrpc-fixture-server.py's
⍝ four on-demand misbehavior modes against Shell/JsonRpc, proving each
⍝ one is a controllable, repeatable trigger rather than something only
⍝ reasoned about. Does NOT attempt to fix anything found here — any
⍝ surprising behavior is just reported, and tracked as a TODO.md item
⍝ if it looks like a real gap (see TODO.md's Shell/JSON-RPC layer
⍝ sections for what this run surfaced).
⎕IO←1
⎕FIX'file://D:/devel/mcp-client/src/Shell.dyalog'
⎕FIX'file://D:/devel/mcp-client/src/JsonRpc.dyalog'

cmd←'python' 'D:\devel\mcp-client\examples\toy-jsonrpc-fixture-server.py'

⍝ --- Sanity: ordinary echo still works against the fixture server ---
h←JsonRpc.Connect cmd
r←h JsonRpc.Call('echo'(text:'sanity'))
⎕←'sanity echo -> ',r.result
JsonRpc.Disconnect h

⍝ --- Mode 1: crash — server exits uncleanly instead of responding ---
h←JsonRpc.Connect cmd
:Trap 999
    r←h JsonRpc.Call('crash'(code:3))
    ⎕←'FAIL: expected a signal, got a response instead'
:Else
    ⎕←'crash -> signaled ok: ',⎕DM
    ⎕←'  Shell.Status after crash=',h.Shell.Status
    ⎕←'  Shell.ExitCode after crash=',⍕h.Shell.ExitCode
:EndTrap
Shell.Stop h.Shell ⍝ already exited; must still be safe to call

⍝ --- Mode 2: garbage — malformed JSON instead of a real response ---
h←JsonRpc.Connect cmd
:Trap 999
    r←h JsonRpc.Call'garbage'
    ⎕←'FAIL: expected a signal, got a response instead'
:Else
    ⎕←'garbage -> signaled ok: ',⎕DM
:EndTrap
⍝ The process itself is still alive (only the response line was bad) —
⍝ confirm the connection can still be used/torn down cleanly.
⎕←'  Shell.Status after garbage=',h.Shell.Status
JsonRpc.Disconnect h

⍝ --- Mode 3: hang — server never responds; must time out ---
h←JsonRpc.Connect cmd
h.Timeout←2
:Trap 999
    r←h JsonRpc.Call'hang'
    ⎕←'FAIL: expected a timeout signal'
:Else
    ⎕←'hang -> timeout signaled ok: ',⎕DM
:EndTrap
Shell.Stop h.Shell

⍝ --- Mode 4: burst — N unsolicited notifications ahead of the real response ---
h←JsonRpc.Connect cmd
r←h JsonRpc.Call('burst'(count:8 ⋄ text:'stress'))
⎕←'burst response -> ',r.result,' (id=',(⍕r.id),')'
⎕←'  notifications queued: ',⍕≢h.Notifications
⎕←'  all burst/notice: ',⍕∧/'burst/notice'∘≡¨h.Notifications.method
⎕←'  n values in order: ',⍕∊h.Notifications.params.n
JsonRpc.Disconnect h

⎕←'done'
⎕OFF
